## Tableau
For Tableau discovery, synchronization or rebuild guidance, call
`load_skill(skill_name="tableau")` before the CLI. Read its `references/sync.md`
before writing a source snapshot.
For dashboard context/metric construction or reconstruction in Datus, the main
agent MUST first load the available `dashboard-bootstrap` skill and then the
available `tableau` skill and its `references/rebuild.md` as platform guidance
before generation.
`dashboard-bootstrap` is the single orchestration entry; it selects outputs and
loads its references on demand. If it is unavailable, report the host capability
gap. Inside `gen_visual_dashboard`, load `dashboard-bootstrap` and `tableau`
to register supporting-file roots, then read only the references needed for the
exact parent handoff; do not restart orchestration or author metrics.
A URL conversion authorizes necessary additive metric creation through the common
workflow; honor an explicit existing-metrics-only restriction. Complete required
metric authoring and validation before visual generation.
The plugin produces source/processing evidence; it does not deploy or run ETL.

Use `datus tableau sync inspect PATH --summary` for a bounded, fully verified
source overview. Local `datus tableau plan --flow FLOW --output DIR` writes derived
SELECT models and reports; `datus tableau rebuild --bundle ... --bindings ...
--metric-catalog ...` prints a DOSI preflight. These managed offline commands do not
require Tableau authentication. Target metric SQL/results still require actual
DOSI discovery and successful artifact-tool trial queries.

`datus tableau context export-dashboard DASHBOARD_ID` snapshots one dashboard's
reviewable sources into the project workspace (under `reference_sql/tableau`),
mirroring the other BI plugins. `datus tableau api call PATH --param KEY=VALUE`
is a read-only, same-origin escape hatch for untyped REST resources the typed
commands do not cover; it never mutates server state.

